  "description": "Industry vocabulary for manufacturers: manufacturing orders, routings and operations, work centres, scrap, yield and rework, WIP, finished goods and raw material, downtime and changeover, plants and shifts. Expands the warehouse's SPELLINGS (SCRP, YLD, WCTR, DWNTM, PLNT) and leaves the acronyms people actually say (BOM, MRP, OEE, WIP, COGS) alone. Carries the production date roles -- planned and actual start and finish, release, reported -- under the column names a manufacturing mart gives them. Carries no table or column dictionary, so it never competes with the ERP pack your database's naming detects; select it alongside that pack.",
